  "correct": "C",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Expand before differentiating",
      "body": "<p>Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></math> with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Expanding a squared rational expression can turn differentiation into the power rule.",
      "pitfall": "Squaring a difference includes the middle term; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\">&#x00028;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"true\" fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Write <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></math> as three powers of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l01",
          "reminder": "Expanding a squared rational expression can turn differentiation into the power rule."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Differentiate the powers twice",
      "body": "<p>The expansion is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>n</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> once, then again.</p>",
      "recap": "The second derivative is obtained by differentiating the first derivative.",
      "pitfall": "Do not substitute <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> before differentiating: that would remove the variable.",
      "pause": "Find <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l18",
          "reminder": "The second derivative is obtained by differentiating the first derivative."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Evaluate the second derivative only",
      "body": "<p>Apply the power rule a second time to every term of your first derivative. Check the new coefficients and signs, then substitute the requested input.</p>",
      "recap": "Finish the differentiation before evaluating the requested input.",
      "pitfall": "The sign of the middle term remains negative in the second derivative.",
      "pause": "Finish the second differentiation, then substitute the requested input and combine the terms.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l18",
          "reminder": "Finish the differentiation before evaluating the requested input."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Therefore <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>f</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi><mi>&#x02032;</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>24</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>24</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.</p><p>At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>, this is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>24</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p><strong>Answer C.</strong></p>",
